{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory resolved the major medication/infusion confusion and built a practical follow-up workflow, with caregiver teach-back. However, the doctor never assessed or escalated gastrointestinal bleeding warning signs such as melena, hematemesis, hematochezia, pallor, dizziness, or fainting despite the authored RC1/RC2 requirements. This is a discoverable, actionable, serious responsibility-chain omission, so the deterministic grade is 1 regardless of later strengths or completed high-order work.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00251",
        "explanation": "The doctor allowed continued home observation based on a red-flag list that did not include GI bleeding risk assessment/escalation.",
        "quote": "继续在家观察即可"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00272",
        "explanation": "The doctor treated the plan as understood and executable for the family.",
        "quote": "有紧急情况直接急诊"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The plan was traceable and executable for medication avoidance, lumbar-puncture monitoring, and follow-up verification, but closure was unsafe because required GI bleeding screening and emergency thresholds were never covered before home observation was endorsed.",
